  "query_preview": "/Tuesday through Saturday/...\nBy Tuesday, deep troughing and strong negative height anomalies \nwill amplify and intensify along the west coast, however confidence\nin the timing and depth of this feature continues to be low to \nmoderate. The deterministic's have started to come into better \nagreement compared to 24 hrs ago but still show key differences. \nThe ECMWF forecast continues to show a slightly slower system \nhowever much shallower than before. Meanwhile the GFS deterministic\nremains mostly unchanged, with the exception of now leaning towards\na more positively tilted trough than compared to the ECMWF, and \nthe previous GFS runs, spreading out any vorticity advection and \nhindering better chances for storm development. Even with these \ndifferences compared to previous runs, the ECMWF continues to \nforecast a more more robust rainfall scenario in comparison to the\nGFS. Either way, Wednesday and Thursday continue to be the best \nwindow for rainfall potential, while pattern recognition and some \ninstability parameters suggest the potential for strong \nthunderstorms ahead of the shortwave passage. Lingering PoPs \ncontinue into Friday morning before expecting to dry out by the \nweekend. \n\nAdditionally, with the uncertainty of this next system remaining,\na wide spread in NBM temperatures continue throughout the week, \nmost notably on Thursday with a spread of 11 degrees between the \n25th and 75th percentile. Even with this large of spread below \nnormal highs are likely late this week heading into the weekend.",
